         {
          TabViewBox[{{1,"\<\"Raw\"\>"->
           FrameBox[
            FrameBox[Cell[BoxData[
              PaneBox[
               
               PaneBox["\<\"/create_nb\\n# Toroidal Closure / Dimensional \
Stability Framework\\n\\n## Phase 2 Notebook: Toroidal Geometry Module and \
Closure Residual\\n\\nThis notebook builds **Section 2 only**: a \
mathematically explicit toroidal geometry module for the smallest candidate \
scale. It focuses on:\\n\\n- symbolic torus parameterization,\\n- induced \
metric and area element,\\n- periodic closure constraints,\\n- toroidal \
closure functionals and residuals,\\n- normalization tests,\\n- and a compact \
interactive exploration interface.\\n\\nIt does **not** identify the \
resulting modes with particles or other physical \
observables.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Precision policy and \
assumptions\\n\\n```wl\\nClearAll[setToroidalFrameworkPrecision];\\n\\\
nsetToroidalFrameworkPrecision[] := (\\n  $Assumptions = Element[\\n      \
{majorRadius, minorRadius, u, v, amp, alpha, beta, closureTargetValue},\\n    \
  Reals\\n    ] && majorRadius > 0 && minorRadius > 0 && majorRadius > \
minorRadius &&\\n    0 <= u <= 2 Pi && 0 <= v <= 2 Pi && alpha > 0 && beta >= \
0;\\n  $MaxExtraPrecision = \
1000;\\n)\\n\\nsetToroidalFrameworkPrecision[];\\n```\\n\\nAs in Phase 1, \
exact ``WorkingPrecision -> Infinity`` is not generally executable for \
numerical integration. This module therefore uses:\\n\\n- exact symbolic \
computation where possible,\\n- otherwise high finite precision,\\n- with \
explicit residual and convergence checks.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Smallest-scale \
geometric parameters\\n\\nWe keep the scale bookkeeping separate from the \
torus geometry so that the module stays \
reusable.\\n\\n```wl\\nClearAll[goldenPhi, planckLength, smallestScaleIndex, \
scaleLength];\\n\\ngoldenPhi = (1 + Sqrt[5]) / 2;\\nplanckLength = \
Quantity[1.616255*10^-35, \\\"Meters\\\"];\\nsmallestScaleIndex = \
0;\\n\\nscaleLength[n_Integer ? NonNegative] := UnitSimplify[planckLength \
goldenPhi^n];\\n```\\n\\nFor the toroidal module we work primarily in \
**dimensionless coordinates**, and only optionally attach units \
later.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. Toroidal parameterization\\n\\nWe define the \
standard embedded torus in $$\\\\mathbb{R}^3$$ with major radius $$R$$ and \
minor radius $$r$$:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\mathbf{x}(u,v) = \\\\{(R + r \\\\cos v) \
\\\\cos u,\\\\ (R + r \\\\cos v) \\\\sin u,\\\\ r \\\\sin \
v\\\\}\\n$$\\n\\nwith both angles periodic on \
$$[0,2\\\\pi]$$.\\n\\n```wl\\nClearAll[torusEmbedding];\\n\\ntorusEmbedding[\
majorRadius_, minorRadius_] :=\\n  Function[{u, v}, {\\n    (majorRadius + \
minorRadius Cos[v]) Cos[u],\\n    (majorRadius + minorRadius Cos[v]) \
Sin[u],\\n    minorRadius Sin[v]\\n  }];\\n```\\n\\nBasic periodic closure \
identities:\\n\\n```wl\\nClearAll[toroidalPeriodicClosureRules, \
toroidalPeriodicClosureQ];\\n\\ntoroidalPeriodicClosureRules = {\\n  Cos[x_ + \
2 Pi] :> Cos[x],\\n  Sin[x_ + 2 Pi] :> \
Sin[x]\\n};\\n\\ntoroidalPeriodicClosureQ[majorRadius_, minorRadius_] := \
Module[\\n  {embed},\\n  embed = torusEmbedding[majorRadius, minorRadius];\\n \
 Simplify[\\n    embed[u + 2 Pi, v] == embed[u, v] && embed[u, v + 2 Pi] == \
embed[u, v],\\n    Assumptions -> $Assumptions\\n  \
]\\n];\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. Tangent vectors, metric, and area element\\n\
\\nWe compute the induced geometry directly from the \
embedding.\\n\\n```wl\\nClearAll[torusTangentU, torusTangentV, \
torusMetricMatrix, torusAreaElement];\\n\\ntorusTangentU[majorRadius_, \
minorRadius_] := Module[\\n  {embed = torusEmbedding[majorRadius, \
minorRadius]},\\n  Function[{u, v}, D[embed[u, v], \
u]]\\n];\\n\\ntorusTangentV[majorRadius_, minorRadius_] := Module[\\n  {embed \
= torusEmbedding[majorRadius, minorRadius]},\\n  Function[{u, v}, D[embed[u, \
v], v]]\\n];\\n\\ntorusMetricMatrix[majorRadius_, minorRadius_] := Module[\\n \
 {xu, xv},\\n  xu = torusTangentU[majorRadius, minorRadius][u, v];\\n  xv = \
torusTangentV[majorRadius, minorRadius][u, v];\\n  Simplify[\\n    {{xu.xu, \
xu.xv}, {xv.xu, xv.xv}},\\n    Assumptions -> $Assumptions\\n  \
]\\n];\\n\\ntorusAreaElement[majorRadius_, minorRadius_] := Simplify[\\n  \
Sqrt[Det[torusMetricMatrix[majorRadius, minorRadius]]],\\n  Assumptions -> \
$Assumptions\\n];\\n```\\n\\nFor a standard torus this simplifies to:\\n\\n$$\
\\n\\\\sqrt{\\\\det g} = r (R + r \\\\cos v)\\n$$\\n\\nwhich leads to the \
exact surface area\\n\\n$$\\nA = 4 \\\\pi^2 R r\\n$$\\n\\nimplemented \
below.\\n\\n```wl\\nClearAll[torusSurfaceArea];\\n\\ntorusSurfaceArea[\
majorRadius_, minorRadius_] := FullSimplify[\\n  Integrate[\\n    \
torusAreaElement[majorRadius, minorRadius],\\n    {u, 0, 2 Pi}, {v, 0, 2 Pi},\
\\n    Assumptions -> $Assumptions\\n  ],\\n  Assumptions -> \
$Assumptions\\n];\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. Scalar fields on the \
torus\\n\\nWe define a Fourier-mode basis respecting toroidal periodicity:\\n\
\\n$$\\n\\\\psi_{m,n}(u,v) = a\\\\, e^{-\\\\alpha \\\\cos v}\\\\, e^{i(mu + \
nv)}\\n$$\\n\\nFor closure tests based on $$|\\\\psi|^2$$, the phase part is \
periodic and the amplitude envelope remains well \
defined.\\n\\n```wl\\nClearAll[toroidalMode];\\n\\ntoroidalMode[m_Integer, \
n_Integer, amp_, alpha_: 0] :=\\n  Function[{u, v}, amp Exp[-alpha Cos[v]] \
Exp[I (m u + n v)]];\\n```\\n\\nA real-valued mode alternative is sometimes \
useful:\\n\\n```wl\\nClearAll[toroidalRealMode];\\n\\ntoroidalRealMode[m_\
Integer, n_Integer, amp_, alpha_: 0, beta_: 0] :=\\n  Function[{u, v}, amp \
Exp[-alpha Cos[v]] Cos[m u + n v + beta]];\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Toroidal \
closure functional\\n\\nWe now define a concrete closure functional over the \
torus surface:\\n\\n$$\\nC[\\\\psi] = \
\\\\int_{0}^{2\\\\pi}\\\\!\\\\int_{0}^{2\\\\pi} |\\\\psi(u,v)|^2 \\\\, \
\\\\sqrt{\\\\det g(u,v)} \\\\, du \\\\, \
dv\\n$$\\n\\n```wl\\nClearAll[toroidalClosureFunctional];\\n\\\
ntoroidalClosureFunctional[psi_, majorRadius_, minorRadius_, wp_: 80] := \
NIntegrate[\\n  Evaluate[Abs[psi[u, v]]^2 torusAreaElement[majorRadius, \
minorRadius]],\\n  {u, 0, 2 Pi}, {v, 0, 2 Pi},\\n  WorkingPrecision -> wp,\\n \
 AccuracyGoal -> 30,\\n  PrecisionGoal -> 30,\\n  Method -> \
{\\\"GlobalAdaptive\\\", \\\"SymbolicProcessing\\\" -> 0}\\n];\\n```\\n\\nFor \
exact symbolic work, we also define a symbolic version where \
possible:\\n\\n```wl\\nClearAll[toroidalClosureFunctionalExact];\\n\\\
ntoroidalClosureFunctionalExact[psi_, majorRadius_, minorRadius_] := \
FullSimplify[\\n  Integrate[\\n    Evaluate[ComplexExpand[Abs[psi[u, v]]^2] \
torusAreaElement[majorRadius, minorRadius]],\\n    {u, 0, 2 Pi}, {v, 0, 2 \
Pi},\\n    Assumptions -> $Assumptions\\n  ],\\n  Assumptions -> $Assumptions\
\\n];\\n```\\n\\nResidual against a target closure \
value:\\n\\n```wl\\nClearAll[toroidalClosureResidual];\\n\\\
ntoroidalClosureResidual[psi_, majorRadius_, minorRadius_, \
closureTargetValue_, wp_: 80] :=\\n  N[toroidalClosureFunctional[psi, \
majorRadius, minorRadius, wp] - closureTargetValue, \
wp];\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Exact normalization of a base mode\\n\\nTake \
the simplest complex toroidal mode with no angular winding and a constant \
envelope:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\psi_{0,0}(u,v) = \
a\\n$$\\n\\nThen\\n\\n$$\\nC[\\\\psi_{0,0}] = |a|^2 A_{\\\\mathrm{torus}} = \
|a|^2 4\\\\pi^2 R r\\n$$\\n\\nso exact normalization to a prescribed target \
$$c_*$$ is:\\n\\n$$\\na = \\\\pm \\\\sqrt{\\\\frac{c_*}{4\\\\pi^2 R \
r}}\\n$$\\n\\n```wl\\nClearAll[constantToroidalMode, \
closureAmplitudeRule];\\n\\nconstantToroidalMode[amp_] := Function[{u, v}, \
amp];\\n\\nclosureAmplitudeRule[majorRadius_, minorRadius_, \
closureTargetValue_] := Solve[\\n  amp^2 torusSurfaceArea[majorRadius, \
minorRadius] == closureTargetValue,\\n  amp,\\n  \
Reals\\n];\\n```\\n\\nNormalized mode \
constructor:\\n\\n```wl\\nClearAll[normalizedConstantToroidalMode];\\n\\\
nnormalizedConstantToroidalMode[majorRadius_, minorRadius_, \
closureTargetValue_] := Module[\\n  {ampRule},\\n  ampRule = \
First[closureAmplitudeRule[majorRadius, minorRadius, closureTargetValue]];\\n \
 Function[{u, v}, amp /. ampRule]\\n];\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Closure \
mismatch and geometric closure tests\\n\\nWe separate three notions:\\n\\n1. \
**Embedding closure**: periodic position matching.\\n2. **Field closure**: \
periodic field matching.\\n3. **Integrated closure**: functional matches \
target value.\\n\\n```wl\\nClearAll[fieldPeriodicClosureQ, \
integratedClosureResidual];\\n\\nfieldPeriodicClosureQ[psi_] := Simplify[\\n  \
psi[u + 2 Pi, v] == psi[u, v] && psi[u, v + 2 Pi] == psi[u, v],\\n  \
Assumptions -> $Assumptions\\n];\\n\\nintegratedClosureResidual[psi_, \
majorRadius_, minorRadius_, closureTargetValue_, wp_: 80] :=\\n  \
toroidalClosureResidual[psi, majorRadius, minorRadius, closureTargetValue, \
wp];\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Geometric and analytic \
diagnostics\\n\\n```wl\\nClearAll[toroidalGeometrySummary];\\n\\\
ntoroidalGeometrySummary[majorRadius_, minorRadius_] := <|\\n  \
\\\"Embedding\\\" -> HoldForm[torusEmbedding[majorRadius, minorRadius][u, \
v]],\\n  \\\"Metric\\\" -> torusMetricMatrix[majorRadius, minorRadius],\\n  \
\\\"AreaElement\\\" -> torusAreaElement[majorRadius, minorRadius],\\n  \
\\\"SurfaceArea\\\" -> torusSurfaceArea[majorRadius, minorRadius],\\n  \
\\\"PeriodicClosureQ\\\" -> toroidalPeriodicClosureQ[majorRadius, \
minorRadius]\\n|>;\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Precision-refinement utility \
for closure computations\\n\\nThis gives an explicit \
convergence-under-precision scaffold for the toroidal closure \
functional.\\n\\n```wl\\nClearAll[closurePrecisionStudy];\\n\\\
nclosurePrecisionStudy[psi_, majorRadius_, minorRadius_, precisions_List] := \
Module[\\n  {values},\\n  values = AssociationThread[\\n    precisions,\\n    \
toroidalClosureFunctional[psi, majorRadius, minorRadius, #] & /@ \
precisions\\n  ];\\n  <|\\n    \\\"Values\\\" -> values,\\n    \
\\\"PairwiseDifferences\\\" -> AssociationThread[\\n      \
Rest[precisions],\\n      MapThread[\\n        Abs[#1 - #2] &,\\n        \
{Most[Values[values]], Rest[Values[values]]}\\n      ]\\n    ]\\n  \
|>\\n];\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Smallest-scale toroidal tests\\n\\nWe \
define a self-contained test suite for the geometry \
module.\\n\\n```wl\\nClearAll[smallestScaleToroidalTestSuite];\\n\\\
nsmallestScaleToroidalTestSuite[] := Module[\\n  {\\n    majorRadius = \
3/2,\\n    minorRadius = 1/2,\\n    closureTargetValue = goldenPhi^-13,\\n    \
normalizedPsi,\\n    ampRule\\n  },\\n\\n  ampRule = \
First[closureAmplitudeRule[majorRadius, minorRadius, closureTargetValue]];\\n \
 normalizedPsi = normalizedConstantToroidalMode[majorRadius, minorRadius, \
closureTargetValue];\\n\\n  TestReport[{\\n\\n    VerificationTest[\\n      \
toroidalPeriodicClosureQ[majorRadius, minorRadius],\\n      True,\\n      \
TestID -> \\\"Toroidal embedding periodic closure\\\"\\n    ],\\n\\n    \
VerificationTest[\\n      torusMetricMatrix[majorRadius, minorRadius] === \
{{(majorRadius + minorRadius Cos[v])^2, 0}, {0, minorRadius^2}},\\n      \
True,\\n      TestID -> \\\"Induced metric matrix\\\"\\n    ],\\n\\n    \
VerificationTest[\\n      FullSimplify[\\n        \
torusAreaElement[majorRadius, minorRadius],\\n        Assumptions -> \
$Assumptions\\n      ] === minorRadius (majorRadius + minorRadius Cos[v]),\\n \
     True,\\n      TestID -> \\\"Toroidal area element\\\"\\n    ],\\n\\n    \
VerificationTest[\\n      FullSimplify[\\n        \
torusSurfaceArea[majorRadius, minorRadius],\\n        Assumptions -> \
$Assumptions\\n      ] === 4 Pi^2 majorRadius minorRadius,\\n      True,\\n   \
   TestID -> \\\"Toroidal surface area\\\"\\n    ],\\n\\n    \
VerificationTest[\\n      fieldPeriodicClosureQ[toroidalMode[1, 2, amp, \
alpha]],\\n      True,\\n      TestID -> \\\"Toroidal complex mode \
periodicity\\\"\\n    ],\\n\\n    VerificationTest[\\n      FullSimplify[\\n  \
      amp^2 torusSurfaceArea[majorRadius, minorRadius] /. ampRule - \
closureTargetValue,\\n        Assumptions -> $Assumptions\\n      ] == 0,\\n  \
    True,\\n      TestID -> \\\"Exact closure amplitude normalization\\\"\\n  \
  ],\\n\\n    VerificationTest[\\n      \
Chop[integratedClosureResidual[normalizedPsi, majorRadius, minorRadius, \
closureTargetValue, 80], 10^-40] == 0,\\n      True,\\n      TestID -> \
\\\"Numerical integrated closure residual\\\"\\n    ]\\n\\n  }]\\n];\\n```\\n\
\\n---\\n\\n## 12. Smallest-scale toroidal framework \
summary\\n\\n```wl\\nClearAll[smallestScaleToroidalFramework];\\n\\\
nsmallestScaleToroidalFramework[] := Module[\\n  {\\n    majorRadius = \
3/2,\\n    minorRadius = 1/2,\\n    closureTargetValue = goldenPhi^-13\\n  },\
\\n  <|\\n    \\\"FrameworkVersion\\\" -> \\\"Phase2.ToroidalGeometry\\\",\\n \
   \\\"ScaleIndex\\\" -> smallestScaleIndex,\\n    \\\"Geometry\\\" -> \
toroidalGeometrySummary[majorRadius, minorRadius],\\n    \
\\\"ClosureTarget\\\" -> closureTargetValue,\\n    \\\"ClosureAmplitudeRule\\\
\" -> closureAmplitudeRule[majorRadius, minorRadius, closureTargetValue],\\n  \
  \\\"Tests\\\" -> smallestScaleToroidalTestSuite[]\\n  \
|>\\n];\\n```\\n\\nRun the framework \
summary:\\n\\n```wl\\nsmallestScaleToroidalFramework[]\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## \
13. Interactive exploration interface\\n\\nThis interface lets you explore \
torus geometry, a simple periodic mode, and the corresponding closure \
functional.\\n\\n```wl\\nManipulate[\\n Module[\\n  {\\n    psi, area, \
closureValue, residualValue, plot3D\\n  },\\n\\n  psi = toroidalMode[m, n, \
amp, alpha];\\n  area = torusSurfaceArea[majorRadius, minorRadius];\\n  \
closureValue = toroidalClosureFunctional[psi, majorRadius, minorRadius, \
wp];\\n  residualValue = N[closureValue - closureTargetValue, wp];\\n\\n  \
plot3D = ParametricPlot3D[\\n    Evaluate[torusEmbedding[majorRadius, \
minorRadius][u, v]],\\n    {u, 0, 2 Pi}, {v, 0, 2 Pi},\\n    Mesh -> None,\\n \
   PlotPoints -> 50,\\n    ColorFunction -> Function[{x, y, z, uu, vv}, \
ColorData[\\\"SolarColors\\\"][Rescale[Re[psi[uu, vv]], {-Abs[amp] \
Exp[alpha], Abs[amp] Exp[alpha]}]]],\\n    ColorFunctionScaling -> False,\\n  \
  Boxed -> False,\\n    Axes -> False,\\n    PlotLabel -> Row[{\\\"Closure = \
\\\", NumberForm[closureValue, {12, 8}], \\\", Residual = \\\", \
NumberForm[residualValue, {12, 8}]}]\\n  ];\\n\\n  Column[{\\n    \
Row[{\\\"Surface area: \\\", area}],\\n    Row[{\\\"Field periodic: \\\", \
fieldPeriodicClosureQ[psi]}],\\n    plot3D\\n  }]\\n ],\\n {{majorRadius, \
1.5, \\\"Major radius\\\"}, 0.6, 3, Appearance -> \\\"Labeled\\\"},\\n \
{{minorRadius, 0.5, \\\"Minor radius\\\"}, 0.1, 1.2, Appearance -> \
\\\"Labeled\\\"},\\n Delimiter,\\n {{m, 1, \\\"Mode m\\\"}, 0, 6, 1, \
Appearance -> \\\"Labeled\\\"},\\n {{n, 1, \\\"Mode n\\\"}, 0, 6, 1, \
Appearance -> \\\"Labeled\\\"},\\n {{amp, 0.1, \\\"Amplitude\\\"}, 0, 2, \
Appearance -> \\\"Labeled\\\"},\\n {{alpha, 0, \\\"Envelope alpha\\\"}, 0, 2, \
Appearance -> \\\"Labeled\\\"},\\n Delimiter,\\n {{closureTargetValue, \
goldenPhi^-13, \\\"Closure target\\\"}, 10^-6, 1, Appearance -> \\\"Labeled\\\
\"},\\n {{wp, 50, \\\"Working precision\\\"}, {30, 50, 80, 100}},\\n \
SaveDefinitions -> True\\n]\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 14. Recommended next \
step\\n\\nAfter this toroidal geometry module, the next logically clean \
addition is:\\n\\n1. add a **field action on the torus** using the induced \
metric,\\n2. derive the corresponding Euler\[Dash]Lagrange equations,\\n3. \
linearize around a background toroidal mode,\\n4. and then compute the \
toroidal eigenspectrum.\\n\\nThat would connect this notebook cleanly back to \
the Phase 1 Layer 1 refinement \
path.\\n\\n/exec\\nRESULT\\nNotebookObject[\\\"de414580-0272-ad40-8931-\
