                    StripOnInput->False,
                    FontSize->11],
                    FrameMargins->{{5, 5}, {1, 1}}],
                   Background->LightDarkSwitched[
                    GrayLevel[0.95], 
                    GrayLevel[0.15295]],
                   ItemSize->Fit,
                   StripOnInput->False]},
                 {
                  FrameBox[
                   TagBox[GridBox[{
                    {"\<\"content\"\>", 
                    InterpretationBox[
                    
                    DynamicModuleBox[{
                    Wolfram`Chatbook`ResourceFunctions`ClickToCopy`cell$$}, 
                    TagBox[
                    TagBox[
                    PaneSelectorBox[{False->
                    
                    FrameBox["\<\"# Update for Notebook ``Untitled \
9``\\n\\n## Linearization and Eigenspectrum Tests Patch\\n\\nPaste the \
following cells into **Untitled 9** after the toroidal geometry/closure \
section. This adds:\\n\\n- linearized scalar stability model,\\n- analytic \
flat-torus proxy eigenvalues,\\n- numerical periodic-grid eigenspectrum,\\n- \
resolution-convergence tests,\\n- and an interactive exploration \
block.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Linearized toroidal model\\n\\nWe introduce a \
scalar surrogate energy on the torus and linearize about a constant \
background mode. For a quartic local term, the linearized operator takes the \
form\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\mathcal{L}_{\\\\mathrm{lin}}\\\\,\\\\delta\\\\psi = \
-\\\\Delta\\\\,\\\\delta\\\\psi + \
\\\\mu_{\\\\mathrm{eff}}\\\\,\\\\delta\\\\psi\\n$$\\n\\nwith\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\mu_\
{\\\\mathrm{eff}} = m_0^2 + 12\\\\lambda\\\\psi_0^2\\n$$\\n\\nwhere ``psi0`` \
is the background value.\\n\\n```wl\\nClearAll[\\n  effectiveMassTerm,\\n  \
flatTorusEigenvalue,\\n  flatTorusFrequency,\\n  undampedModeQ,\\n  \
stableFlatTorusModes\\n];\\n\\neffectiveMassTerm[massTerm_, coupling_, \
backgroundValue_] :=\\n  Simplify[massTerm + 12 coupling backgroundValue^2, \
Assumptions -> $Assumptions];\\n\\nflatTorusEigenvalue[\\n  m_Integer, \
n_Integer,\\n  majorRadius_, minorRadius_,\\n  massTerm_, coupling_, \
backgroundValue_\\n] := Simplify[\\n  m^2/majorRadius^2 + n^2/minorRadius^2 + \
effectiveMassTerm[massTerm, coupling, backgroundValue],\\n  Assumptions -> \
$Assumptions\\n];\\n\\nflatTorusFrequency[\\n  m_Integer, n_Integer,\\n  \
majorRadius_, minorRadius_,\\n  massTerm_, coupling_, backgroundValue_\\n] := \
Simplify[\\n  Sqrt[flatTorusEigenvalue[m, n, majorRadius, minorRadius, \
massTerm, coupling, backgroundValue]],\\n  Assumptions -> \
$Assumptions\\n];\\n\\nundampedModeQ[\\n  m_Integer, n_Integer,\\n  \
majorRadius_, minorRadius_,\\n  massTerm_, coupling_, backgroundValue_\\n] := \
Simplify[\\n  flatTorusEigenvalue[m, n, majorRadius, minorRadius, massTerm, \
coupling, backgroundValue] > 0,\\n  Assumptions -> \
$Assumptions\\n];\\n\\nstableFlatTorusModes[\\n  maxMode_Integer ? \
NonNegative,\\n  majorRadius_, minorRadius_,\\n  massTerm_, coupling_, \
backgroundValue_\\n] :=\\n  Select[\\n    Flatten[Table[{m, n}, {m, 0, \
maxMode}, {n, 0, maxMode}], 1],\\n    TrueQ[\\n      undampedModeQ[#[[1]], \
#[[2]], majorRadius, minorRadius, massTerm, coupling, backgroundValue]\\n    \
] &\\n  ];\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Periodic-grid operator and numerical \
eigensystem\\n\\nThis is a numerical proxy for a toroidal Laplacian with \
periodic boundary conditions on a rectangular parameter \
domain.\\n\\n```wl\\nClearAll[\\n  periodicSecondDifferenceMatrix,\\n  \
flatTorusOperatorMatrix,\\n  \
flatTorusEigenSystem\\n];\\n\\nperiodicSecondDifferenceMatrix[\\n  \
nPts_Integer ? Positive,\\n  domainLength_: 2 Pi,\\n  wp_: 80\\n] := \
Module[{h, rules},\\n  h = SetPrecision[domainLength/nPts, wp];\\n  rules = \
Join[\\n    Table[{i, i} -> SetPrecision[-2/h^2, wp], {i, nPts}],\\n    \
Table[{i, i + 1} -> SetPrecision[1/h^2, wp], {i, 1, nPts - 1}],\\n    \
Table[{i + 1, i} -> SetPrecision[1/h^2, wp], {i, 1, nPts - 1}],\\n    {\\n    \
  {1, nPts} -> SetPrecision[1/h^2, wp],\\n      {nPts, 1} -> \
SetPrecision[1/h^2, wp]\\n    }\\n  ];\\n  SparseArray[rules, {nPts, \
nPts}]\\n];\\n\\nflatTorusOperatorMatrix[\\n  nU_Integer ? Positive,\\n  \
nV_Integer ? Positive,\\n  massEff_,\\n  wp_: 80\\n] := Module[{du2, dv2, \
idU, idV},\\n  du2 = periodicSecondDifferenceMatrix[nU, 2 Pi, wp];\\n  dv2 = \
periodicSecondDifferenceMatrix[nV, 2 Pi, wp];\\n  idU = IdentityMatrix[nU, \
SparseArray];\\n  idV = IdentityMatrix[nV, SparseArray];\\n  N[\\n    \
-KroneckerProduct[du2, idV] - KroneckerProduct[idU, dv2] + massEff \
IdentityMatrix[nU nV, SparseArray],\\n    wp\\n  \
]\\n];\\n\\nflatTorusEigenSystem[\\n  nU_Integer ? Positive,\\n  nV_Integer ? \
Positive,\\n  massTerm_,\\n  coupling_,\\n  backgroundValue_,\\n  \
count_Integer ? Positive,\\n  wp_: 80\\n] := Module[{massEff, vals, vecs},\\n \
 massEff = N[effectiveMassTerm[massTerm, coupling, backgroundValue], wp];\\n  \
{vals, vecs} = Eigensystem[\\n    flatTorusOperatorMatrix[nU, nV, massEff, \
wp],\\n    count,\\n    Method -> {\\\"Arnoldi\\\", \\\"Criteria\\\" -> \
\\\"RealPart\\\"}\\n  ];\\n  {vals, vecs}\\n];\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. \
Eigenspectrum summaries and resolution study\\n\\n```wl\\nClearAll[\\n  \
eigenspectrumSummary,\\n  eigenspectrumResolutionStudy,\\n  \
linearizedToroidalModelSummary\\n];\\n\\neigenspectrumSummary[\\n  \
maxMode_Integer ? NonNegative,\\n  majorRadius_, minorRadius_,\\n  massTerm_, \
coupling_, backgroundValue_\\n] := Association[\\n  Flatten[\\n    Table[\\n  \
    {m, n} -> <|\\n        \\\"Eigenvalue\\\" -> flatTorusEigenvalue[m, n, \
majorRadius, minorRadius, massTerm, coupling, backgroundValue],\\n        \
\\\"Frequency\\\" -> flatTorusFrequency[m, n, majorRadius, minorRadius, \
massTerm, coupling, backgroundValue],\\n        \\\"UndampedQ\\\" -> \
undampedModeQ[m, n, majorRadius, minorRadius, massTerm, coupling, \
backgroundValue]\\n      |>,\\n      {m, 0, maxMode}, {n, 0, maxMode}\\n    \
],\\n    1\\n  ]\\n];\\n\\neigenspectrumResolutionStudy[\\n  \
resolutions_List,\\n  massTerm_, coupling_, backgroundValue_,\\n  \
count_Integer : 8,\\n  wp_: 80\\n] := AssociationThread[\\n  resolutions,\\n  \
(flatTorusEigenSystem[#[[1]], #[[2]], massTerm, coupling, backgroundValue, \
count, wp][[1]] &) /@ \
resolutions\\n];\\n\\nlinearizedToroidalModelSummary[\\n  majorRadius_, \
minorRadius_,\\n  massTerm_, coupling_, backgroundValue_,\\n  maxMode_: 3\\n] \
:= <|\\n  \\\"EffectiveMassTerm\\\" -> effectiveMassTerm[massTerm, coupling, \
backgroundValue],\\n  \\\"StableModes\\\" -> stableFlatTorusModes[maxMode, \
majorRadius, minorRadius, massTerm, coupling, backgroundValue],\\n  \
\\\"ModeSummary\\\" -> eigenspectrumSummary[maxMode, majorRadius, \
minorRadius, massTerm, coupling, \
backgroundValue]\\n|>;\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. Test suite \
extension\\n\\nThis assumes the notebook already defines:\\n\\n- \
``goldenPhi``\\n- ``normalizedConstantToroidalMode``\\n- \
``toroidalPeriodicClosureQ``\\n- \
``fieldPeriodicClosureQ``\\n\\n```wl\\nClearAll[\
smallestScaleLinearizationTestSuite];\\n\\\
nsmallestScaleLinearizationTestSuite[] := Module[\\n  {\\n    majorRadius = \
3/2,\\n    minorRadius = 1/2,\\n    closureTargetValue = goldenPhi^-13,\\n    \
backgroundValue,\\n    massTerm = 1,\\n    coupling = 1/10,\\n    \
normalizedPsi,\\n    eigenvaluesCoarse,\\n    eigenvaluesFine\\n  },\\n\\n  \
normalizedPsi = normalizedConstantToroidalMode[majorRadius, minorRadius, \
closureTargetValue];\\n  backgroundValue = normalizedPsi[0, 0];\\n\\n  \
eigenvaluesCoarse = Sort[Re[flatTorusEigenSystem[8, 8, massTerm, coupling, \
backgroundValue, 6, 60][[1]]]];\\n  eigenvaluesFine = \
Sort[Re[flatTorusEigenSystem[12, 12, massTerm, coupling, backgroundValue, 6, \
60][[1]]]];\\n\\n  TestReport[{\\n\\n    VerificationTest[\\n      \
toroidalPeriodicClosureQ[majorRadius, minorRadius],\\n      True,\\n      \
TestID -> \\\"Toroidal embedding periodic closure\\\"\\n    ],\\n\\n    \
VerificationTest[\\n      fieldPeriodicClosureQ[toroidalMode[2, 3, amp, \
alpha]],\\n      True,\\n      TestID -> \\\"Toroidal mode periodicity\\\"\\n \
   ],\\n\\n    VerificationTest[\\n      FullSimplify[\\n        \
flatTorusEigenvalue[0, 0, majorRadius, minorRadius, massTerm, coupling, \
backgroundValue] ==\\n        effectiveMassTerm[massTerm, coupling, \
backgroundValue],\\n        Assumptions -> $Assumptions\\n      ],\\n      \
True,\\n      TestID -> \\\"Zero mode eigenvalue equals effective mass\\\"\\n \
   ],\\n\\n    VerificationTest[\\n      TrueQ[\\n        \
flatTorusEigenvalue[1, 0, majorRadius, minorRadius, massTerm, coupling, \
backgroundValue] >\\n        flatTorusEigenvalue[0, 0, majorRadius, \
minorRadius, massTerm, coupling, backgroundValue]\\n      ],\\n      True,\\n \
     TestID -> \\\"Nonzero mode exceeds zero mode\\\"\\n    ],\\n\\n    \
VerificationTest[\\n      Length[stableFlatTorusModes[3, majorRadius, \
minorRadius, massTerm, coupling, backgroundValue]] > 0,\\n      True,\\n      \
TestID -> \\\"Stable flat torus modes exist\\\"\\n    ],\\n\\n    \
VerificationTest[\\n      Min[eigenvaluesCoarse] > 0,\\n      True,\\n      \
TestID -> \\\"Coarse-grid eigenvalues positive\\\"\\n    ],\\n\\n    \
VerificationTest[\\n      Max[Abs[eigenvaluesCoarse - eigenvaluesFine[[1 ;; \
Length[eigenvaluesCoarse]]]]] < 10,\\n      True,\\n      TestID -> \
\\\"Resolution refinement remains bounded\\\"\\n    ]\\n\\n  }]\\n];\\n```\\n\
\\nTo run the new \
tests:\\n\\n```wl\\nsmallestScaleLinearizationTestSuite[]\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\\
n## 5. Framework summary extension\\n\\nIf you already have a summary \
association, append a linearization block like \
this:\\n\\n```wl\\nClearAll[smallestScaleToroidalLinearizedFramework];\\n\\\
nsmallestScaleToroidalLinearizedFramework[] := Module[\\n  {\\n    \
majorRadius = 3/2,\\n    minorRadius = 1/2,\\n    closureTargetValue = \
goldenPhi^-13,\\n    normalizedPsi,\\n    backgroundValue,\\n    massTerm = \
1,\\n    coupling = 1/10\\n  },\\n\\n  normalizedPsi = \
normalizedConstantToroidalMode[majorRadius, minorRadius, closureTargetValue];\
\\n  backgroundValue = normalizedPsi[0, 0];\\n\\n  <|\\n    \
\\\"FrameworkVersion\\\" -> \\\"Phase3.ToroidalLinearization\\\",\\n    \
\\\"ScaleIndex\\\" -> 0,\\n    \\\"ClosureTarget\\\" -> \
closureTargetValue,\\n    \\\"BackgroundValue\\\" -> backgroundValue,\\n    \
\\\"LinearizedModel\\\" -> linearizedToroidalModelSummary[\\n      \
majorRadius, minorRadius, massTerm, coupling, backgroundValue, 3\\n    ],\\n  \
  \\\"SampleNumericalEigenvalues\\\" -> flatTorusEigenSystem[\\n      10, 10, \
massTerm, coupling, backgroundValue, 8, 80\\n    ][[1]],\\n    \\\"Tests\\\" \
-> smallestScaleLinearizationTestSuite[]\\n  |>\\n];\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## \
6. Interactive exploration interface\\n\\n```wl\\nManipulate[\\n Module[\\n  \
{\\n    backgroundValue,\\n    eigenTable,\\n    numericalEigenvalues,\\n    \
modePlot\\n  },\\n\\n  backgroundValue = \
normalizedConstantToroidalMode[majorRadius, minorRadius, \
closureTargetValue][0, 0];\\n\\n  eigenTable = Grid[\\n    Prepend[\\n      \
Flatten[\\n        Table[\\n          {\\n            {m, n},\\n            \
N[flatTorusEigenvalue[m, n, majorRadius, minorRadius, massTerm, coupling, \
backgroundValue], 20],\\n            N[flatTorusFrequency[m, n, majorRadius, \
minorRadius, massTerm, coupling, backgroundValue], 20]\\n          },\\n      \
    {m, 0, maxMode}, {n, 0, maxMode}\\n        ],\\n        1\\n      ],\\n   \
   {\\\"Mode\\\", \\\"Eigenvalue\\\", \\\"Frequency\\\"}\\n    ],\\n    Frame \
-> All\\n  ];\\n\\n  numericalEigenvalues = flatTorusEigenSystem[nU, nV, \
massTerm, coupling, backgroundValue, eigenCount, wp][[1]];\\n\\n  modePlot = \
Plot3D[\\n    Evaluate[Re[toroidalMode[modeU, modeV, 1, alpha][u, v]]],\\n    \
{u, 0, 2 Pi}, {v, 0, 2 Pi},\\n    Mesh -> None,\\n    PlotPoints -> 50,\\n    \
ColorFunction -> \\\"SolarColors\\\",\\n    PlotLabel -> Row[{\\\"Re \
mode(\\\", modeU, \\\",\\\", modeV, \\\")\\\"}]\\n  ];\\n\\n  Column[{\\n    \
Row[{\\\"Background value: \\\", N[backgroundValue, 20]}],\\n    \
Row[{\\\"Effective mass term: \\\", N[effectiveMassTerm[massTerm, coupling, \
backgroundValue], 20]}],\\n    Row[{\\\"Numerical eigenvalues: \\\", \
N[numericalEigenvalues, 10]}],\\n    eigenTable,\\n    modePlot\\n  }]\\n \
],\\n {{majorRadius, 1.5, \\\"Major radius\\\"}, 0.6, 3, Appearance -> \
\\\"Labeled\\\"},\\n {{minorRadius, 0.5, \\\"Minor radius\\\"}, 0.1, 1.2, \
Appearance -> \\\"Labeled\\\"},\\n Delimiter,\\n {{closureTargetValue, \
goldenPhi^-13, \\\"Closure target\\\"}, 10^-6, 1, Appearance -> \\\"Labeled\\\
\"},\\n {{massTerm, 1, \\\"Mass term\\\"}, 0, 5, Appearance -> \
\\\"Labeled\\\"},\\n {{coupling, 0.1, \\\"Quartic coupling\\\"}, 0, 2, \
Appearance -> \\\"Labeled\\\"},\\n {{alpha, 0, \\\"Envelope alpha\\\"}, 0, 2, \
Appearance -> \\\"Labeled\\\"},\\n Delimiter,\\n {{maxMode, 2, \\\"Analytic \
max mode\\\"}, 0, 5, 1, Appearance -> \\\"Labeled\\\"},\\n {{modeU, 1, \
\\\"Plot mode m\\\"}, 0, 6, 1, Appearance -> \\\"Labeled\\\"},\\n {{modeV, 1, \
\\\"Plot mode n\\\"}, 0, 6, 1, Appearance -> \\\"Labeled\\\"},\\n \
Delimiter,\\n {{nU, 10, \\\"Grid u\\\"}, 6, 20, 1, Appearance -> \
\\\"Labeled\\\"},\\n {{nV, 10, \\\"Grid v\\\"}, 6, 20, 1, Appearance -> \
\\\"Labeled\\\"},\\n {{eigenCount, 8, \\\"Eigenvalue count\\\"}, 4, 20, 1, \
Appearance -> \\\"Labeled\\\"},\\n {{wp, 60, \\\"Working precision\\\"}, {40, \
60, 80, 100}},\\n SaveDefinitions -> True\\n]\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. \
Recommended next refinement\\n\\nThe next stronger geometric step would be to \
replace the flat-torus proxy operator by a true torus Laplace--Beltrami \
operator derived from the induced metric. That would make the linearization \
geometry-dependent rather than only periodic-domain dependent.\"\>",
                    Background->None,
                    FrameMargins->1,
                    FrameStyle->Dynamic[
                    CurrentValue[Background]],
                    StripOnInput->False], True->
                    FrameBox[
                    
                    StyleBox["\<\"# Update for Notebook ``Untitled \
9``\\n\\n## Linearization and Eigenspectrum Tests Patch\\n\\nPaste the \
following cells into **Untitled 9** after the toroidal geometry/closure \
section. This adds:\\n\\n- linearized scalar stability model,\\n- analytic \
flat-torus proxy eigenvalues,\\n- numerical periodic-grid eigenspectrum,\\n- \
resolution-convergence tests,\\n- and an interactive exploration \
block.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Linearized toroidal model\\n\\nWe introduce a \
scalar surrogate energy on the torus and linearize about a constant \
background mode. For a quartic local term, the linearized operator takes the \
form\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\mathcal{L}_{\\\\mathrm{lin}}\\\\,\\\\delta\\\\psi = \
-\\\\Delta\\\\,\\\\delta\\\\psi + \
\\\\mu_{\\\\mathrm{eff}}\\\\,\\\\delta\\\\psi\\n$$\\n\\nwith\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\mu_\
{\\\\mathrm{eff}} = m_0^2 + 12\\\\lambda\\\\psi_0^2\\n$$\\n\\nwhere ``psi0`` \
is the background value.\\n\\n```wl\\nClearAll[\\n  effectiveMassTerm,\\n  \
flatTorusEigenvalue,\\n  flatTorusFrequency,\\n  undampedModeQ,\\n  \
stableFlatTorusModes\\n];\\n\\neffectiveMassTerm[massTerm_, coupling_, \
backgroundValue_] :=\\n  Simplify[massTerm + 12 coupling backgroundValue^2, \
Assumptions -> $Assumptions];\\n\\nflatTorusEigenvalue[\\n  m_Integer, \
n_Integer,\\n  majorRadius_, minorRadius_,\\n  massTerm_, coupling_, \
backgroundValue_\\n] := Simplify[\\n  m^2/majorRadius^2 + n^2/minorRadius^2 + \
effectiveMassTerm[massTerm, coupling, backgroundValue],\\n  Assumptions -> \
$Assumptions\\n];\\n\\nflatTorusFrequency[\\n  m_Integer, n_Integer,\\n  \
majorRadius_, minorRadius_,\\n  massTerm_, coupling_, backgroundValue_\\n] := \
Simplify[\\n  Sqrt[flatTorusEigenvalue[m, n, majorRadius, minorRadius, \
massTerm, coupling, backgroundValue]],\\n  Assumptions -> \
$Assumptions\\n];\\n\\nundampedModeQ[\\n  m_Integer, n_Integer,\\n  \
majorRadius_, minorRadius_,\\n  massTerm_, coupling_, backgroundValue_\\n] := \
Simplify[\\n  flatTorusEigenvalue[m, n, majorRadius, minorRadius, massTerm, \
coupling, backgroundValue] > 0,\\n  Assumptions -> \
$Assumptions\\n];\\n\\nstableFlatTorusModes[\\n  maxMode_Integer ? \
NonNegative,\\n  majorRadius_, minorRadius_,\\n  massTerm_, coupling_, \
backgroundValue_\\n] :=\\n  Select[\\n    Flatten[Table[{m, n}, {m, 0, \
maxMode}, {n, 0, maxMode}], 1],\\n    TrueQ[\\n      undampedModeQ[#[[1]], \
#[[2]], majorRadius, minorRadius, massTerm, coupling, backgroundValue]\\n    \
] &\\n  ];\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Periodic-grid operator and numerical \
eigensystem\\n\\nThis is a numerical proxy for a toroidal Laplacian with \
periodic boundary conditions on a rectangular parameter \
domain.\\n\\n```wl\\nClearAll[\\n  periodicSecondDifferenceMatrix,\\n  \
flatTorusOperatorMatrix,\\n  \
flatTorusEigenSystem\\n];\\n\\nperiodicSecondDifferenceMatrix[\\n  \
nPts_Integer ? Positive,\\n  domainLength_: 2 Pi,\\n  wp_: 80\\n] := \
Module[{h, rules},\\n  h = SetPrecision[domainLength/nPts, wp];\\n  rules = \
Join[\\n    Table[{i, i} -> SetPrecision[-2/h^2, wp], {i, nPts}],\\n    \
Table[{i, i + 1} -> SetPrecision[1/h^2, wp], {i, 1, nPts - 1}],\\n    \
Table[{i + 1, i} -> SetPrecision[1/h^2, wp], {i, 1, nPts - 1}],\\n    {\\n    \
  {1, nPts} -> SetPrecision[1/h^2, wp],\\n      {nPts, 1} -> \
SetPrecision[1/h^2, wp]\\n    }\\n  ];\\n  SparseArray[rules, {nPts, \
nPts}]\\n];\\n\\nflatTorusOperatorMatrix[\\n  nU_Integer ? Positive,\\n  \
nV_Integer ? Positive,\\n  massEff_,\\n  wp_: 80\\n] := Module[{du2, dv2, \
idU, idV},\\n  du2 = periodicSecondDifferenceMatrix[nU, 2 Pi, wp];\\n  dv2 = \
periodicSecondDifferenceMatrix[nV, 2 Pi, wp];\\n  idU = IdentityMatrix[nU, \
SparseArray];\\n  idV = IdentityMatrix[nV, SparseArray];\\n  N[\\n    \
-KroneckerProduct[du2, idV] - KroneckerProduct[idU, dv2] + massEff \
IdentityMatrix[nU nV, SparseArray],\\n    wp\\n  \
]\\n];\\n\\nflatTorusEigenSystem[\\n  nU_Integer ? Positive,\\n  nV_Integer ? \
Positive,\\n  massTerm_,\\n  coupling_,\\n  backgroundValue_,\\n  \
count_Integer ? Positive,\\n  wp_: 80\\n] := Module[{massEff, vals, vecs},\\n \
 massEff = N[effectiveMassTerm[massTerm, coupling, backgroundValue], wp];\\n  \
{vals, vecs} = Eigensystem[\\n    flatTorusOperatorMatrix[nU, nV, massEff, \
wp],\\n    count,\\n    Method -> {\\\"Arnoldi\\\", \\\"Criteria\\\" -> \
\\\"RealPart\\\"}\\n  ];\\n  {vals, vecs}\\n];\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. \
Eigenspectrum summaries and resolution study\\n\\n```wl\\nClearAll[\\n  \
eigenspectrumSummary,\\n  eigenspectrumResolutionStudy,\\n  \
linearizedToroidalModelSummary\\n];\\n\\neigenspectrumSummary[\\n  \
maxMode_Integer ? NonNegative,\\n  majorRadius_, minorRadius_,\\n  massTerm_, \
coupling_, backgroundValue_\\n] := Association[\\n  Flatten[\\n    Table[\\n  \
    {m, n} -> <|\\n        \\\"Eigenvalue\\\" -> flatTorusEigenvalue[m, n, \
majorRadius, minorRadius, massTerm, coupling, backgroundValue],\\n        \
\\\"Frequency\\\" -> flatTorusFrequency[m, n, majorRadius, minorRadius, \
massTerm, coupling, backgroundValue],\\n        \\\"UndampedQ\\\" -> \
undampedModeQ[m, n, majorRadius, minorRadius, massTerm, coupling, \
backgroundValue]\\n      |>,\\n      {m, 0, maxMode}, {n, 0, maxMode}\\n    \
],\\n    1\\n  ]\\n];\\n\\neigenspectrumResolutionStudy[\\n  \
resolutions_List,\\n  massTerm_, coupling_, backgroundValue_,\\n  \
count_Integer : 8,\\n  wp_: 80\\n] := AssociationThread[\\n  resolutions,\\n  \
(flatTorusEigenSystem[#[[1]], #[[2]], massTerm, coupling, backgroundValue, \
count, wp][[1]] &) /@ \
resolutions\\n];\\n\\nlinearizedToroidalModelSummary[\\n  majorRadius_, \
minorRadius_,\\n  massTerm_, coupling_, backgroundValue_,\\n  maxMode_: 3\\n] \
:= <|\\n  \\\"EffectiveMassTerm\\\" -> effectiveMassTerm[massTerm, coupling, \
backgroundValue],\\n  \\\"StableModes\\\" -> stableFlatTorusModes[maxMode, \
majorRadius, minorRadius, massTerm, coupling, backgroundValue],\\n  \
\\\"ModeSummary\\\" -> eigenspectrumSummary[maxMode, majorRadius, \
minorRadius, massTerm, coupling, \
backgroundValue]\\n|>;\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. Test suite \
extension\\n\\nThis assumes the notebook already defines:\\n\\n- \
``goldenPhi``\\n- ``normalizedConstantToroidalMode``\\n- \
``toroidalPeriodicClosureQ``\\n- \
``fieldPeriodicClosureQ``\\n\\n```wl\\nClearAll[\
smallestScaleLinearizationTestSuite];\\n\\\
nsmallestScaleLinearizationTestSuite[] := Module[\\n  {\\n    majorRadius = \
3/2,\\n    minorRadius = 1/2,\\n    closureTargetValue = goldenPhi^-13,\\n    \
backgroundValue,\\n    massTerm = 1,\\n    coupling = 1/10,\\n    \
normalizedPsi,\\n    eigenvaluesCoarse,\\n    eigenvaluesFine\\n  },\\n\\n  \
normalizedPsi = normalizedConstantToroidalMode[majorRadius, minorRadius, \
closureTargetValue];\\n  backgroundValue = normalizedPsi[0, 0];\\n\\n  \
eigenvaluesCoarse = Sort[Re[flatTorusEigenSystem[8, 8, massTerm, coupling, \
backgroundValue, 6, 60][[1]]]];\\n  eigenvaluesFine = \
Sort[Re[flatTorusEigenSystem[12, 12, massTerm, coupling, backgroundValue, 6, \
60][[1]]]];\\n\\n  TestReport[{\\n\\n    VerificationTest[\\n      \
toroidalPeriodicClosureQ[majorRadius, minorRadius],\\n      True,\\n      \
TestID -> \\\"Toroidal embedding periodic closure\\\"\\n    ],\\n\\n    \
VerificationTest[\\n      fieldPeriodicClosureQ[toroidalMode[2, 3, amp, \
alpha]],\\n      True,\\n      TestID -> \\\"Toroidal mode periodicity\\\"\\n \
   ],\\n\\n    VerificationTest[\\n      FullSimplify[\\n        \
flatTorusEigenvalue[0, 0, majorRadius, minorRadius, massTerm, coupling, \
backgroundValue] ==\\n        effectiveMassTerm[massTerm, coupling, \
backgroundValue],\\n        Assumptions -> $Assumptions\\n      ],\\n      \
True,\\n      TestID -> \\\"Zero mode eigenvalue equals effective mass\\\"\\n \
   ],\\n\\n    VerificationTest[\\n      TrueQ[\\n        \
flatTorusEigenvalue[1, 0, majorRadius, minorRadius, massTerm, coupling, \
backgroundValue] >\\n        flatTorusEigenvalue[0, 0, majorRadius, \
minorRadius, massTerm, coupling, backgroundValue]\\n      ],\\n      True,\\n \
     TestID -> \\\"Nonzero mode exceeds zero mode\\\"\\n    ],\\n\\n    \
VerificationTest[\\n      Length[stableFlatTorusModes[3, majorRadius, \
minorRadius, massTerm, coupling, backgroundValue]] > 0,\\n      True,\\n      \
TestID -> \\\"Stable flat torus modes exist\\\"\\n    ],\\n\\n    \
VerificationTest[\\n      Min[eigenvaluesCoarse] > 0,\\n      True,\\n      \
TestID -> \\\"Coarse-grid eigenvalues positive\\\"\\n    ],\\n\\n    \
VerificationTest[\\n      Max[Abs[eigenvaluesCoarse - eigenvaluesFine[[1 ;; \
Length[eigenvaluesCoarse]]]]] < 10,\\n      True,\\n      TestID -> \
\\\"Resolution refinement remains bounded\\\"\\n    ]\\n\\n  }]\\n];\\n```\\n\
\\nTo run the new \
tests:\\n\\n```wl\\nsmallestScaleLinearizationTestSuite[]\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\\
n## 5. Framework summary extension\\n\\nIf you already have a summary \
association, append a linearization block like \
this:\\n\\n```wl\\nClearAll[smallestScaleToroidalLinearizedFramework];\\n\\\
nsmallestScaleToroidalLinearizedFramework[] := Module[\\n  {\\n    \
majorRadius = 3/2,\\n    minorRadius = 1/2,\\n    closureTargetValue = \
goldenPhi^-13,\\n    normalizedPsi,\\n    backgroundValue,\\n    massTerm = \
1,\\n    coupling = 1/10\\n  },\\n\\n  normalizedPsi = \
normalizedConstantToroidalMode[majorRadius, minorRadius, closureTargetValue];\
\\n  backgroundValue = normalizedPsi[0, 0];\\n\\n  <|\\n    \
\\\"FrameworkVersion\\\" -> \\\"Phase3.ToroidalLinearization\\\",\\n    \
\\\"ScaleIndex\\\" -> 0,\\n    \\\"ClosureTarget\\\" -> \
closureTargetValue,\\n    \\\"BackgroundValue\\\" -> backgroundValue,\\n    \
\\\"LinearizedModel\\\" -> linearizedToroidalModelSummary[\\n      \
majorRadius, minorRadius, massTerm, coupling, backgroundValue, 3\\n    ],\\n  \
  \\\"SampleNumericalEigenvalues\\\" -> flatTorusEigenSystem[\\n      10, 10, \
massTerm, coupling, backgroundValue, 8, 80\\n    ][[1]],\\n    \\\"Tests\\\" \
-> smallestScaleLinearizationTestSuite[]\\n  |>\\n];\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## \
6. Interactive exploration interface\\n\\n```wl\\nManipulate[\\n Module[\\n  \
{\\n    backgroundValue,\\n    eigenTable,\\n    numericalEigenvalues,\\n    \
modePlot\\n  },\\n\\n  backgroundValue = \
normalizedConstantToroidalMode[majorRadius, minorRadius, \
closureTargetValue][0, 0];\\n\\n  eigenTable = Grid[\\n    Prepend[\\n      \
Flatten[\\n        Table[\\n          {\\n            {m, n},\\n            \
N[flatTorusEigenvalue[m, n, majorRadius, minorRadius, massTerm, coupling, \
backgroundValue], 20],\\n            N[flatTorusFrequency[m, n, majorRadius, \
minorRadius, massTerm, coupling, backgroundValue], 20]\\n          },\\n      \
    {m, 0, maxMode}, {n, 0, maxMode}\\n        ],\\n        1\\n      ],\\n   \
   {\\\"Mode\\\", \\\"Eigenvalue\\\", \\\"Frequency\\\"}\\n    ],\\n    Frame \
-> All\\n  ];\\n\\n  numericalEigenvalues = flatTorusEigenSystem[nU, nV, \
massTerm, coupling, backgroundValue, eigenCount, wp][[1]];\\n\\n  modePlot = \
Plot3D[\\n    Evaluate[Re[toroidalMode[modeU, modeV, 1, alpha][u, v]]],\\n    \
{u, 0, 2 Pi}, {v, 0, 2 Pi},\\n    Mesh -> None,\\n    PlotPoints -> 50,\\n    \
ColorFunction -> \\\"SolarColors\\\",\\n    PlotLabel -> Row[{\\\"Re \
mode(\\\", modeU, \\\",\\\", modeV, \\\")\\\"}]\\n  ];\\n\\n  Column[{\\n    \
Row[{\\\"Background value: \\\", N[backgroundValue, 20]}],\\n    \
Row[{\\\"Effective mass term: \\\", N[effectiveMassTerm[massTerm, coupling, \
backgroundValue], 20]}],\\n    Row[{\\\"Numerical eigenvalues: \\\", \
N[numericalEigenvalues, 10]}],\\n    eigenTable,\\n    modePlot\\n  }]\\n \
],\\n {{majorRadius, 1.5, \\\"Major radius\\\"}, 0.6, 3, Appearance -> \
\\\"Labeled\\\"},\\n {{minorRadius, 0.5, \\\"Minor radius\\\"}, 0.1, 1.2, \
Appearance -> \\\"Labeled\\\"},\\n Delimiter,\\n {{closureTargetValue, \
goldenPhi^-13, \\\"Closure target\\\"}, 10^-6, 1, Appearance -> \\\"Labeled\\\
\"},\\n {{massTerm, 1, \\\"Mass term\\\"}, 0, 5, Appearance -> \
\\\"Labeled\\\"},\\n {{coupling, 0.1, \\\"Quartic coupling\\\"}, 0, 2, \
Appearance -> \\\"Labeled\\\"},\\n {{alpha, 0, \\\"Envelope alpha\\\"}, 0, 2, \
Appearance -> \\\"Labeled\\\"},\\n Delimiter,\\n {{maxMode, 2, \\\"Analytic \
max mode\\\"}, 0, 5, 1, Appearance -> \\\"Labeled\\\"},\\n {{modeU, 1, \
\\\"Plot mode m\\\"}, 0, 6, 1, Appearance -> \\\"Labeled\\\"},\\n {{modeV, 1, \
\\\"Plot mode n\\\"}, 0, 6, 1, Appearance -> \\\"Labeled\\\"},\\n \
Delimiter,\\n {{nU, 10, \\\"Grid u\\\"}, 6, 20, 1, Appearance -> \
\\\"Labeled\\\"},\\n {{nV, 10, \\\"Grid v\\\"}, 6, 20, 1, Appearance -> \
\\\"Labeled\\\"},\\n {{eigenCount, 8, \\\"Eigenvalue count\\\"}, 4, 20, 1, \
Appearance -> \\\"Labeled\\\"},\\n {{wp, 60, \\\"Working precision\\\"}, {40, \
60, 80, 100}},\\n SaveDefinitions -> True\\n]\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. \
Recommended next refinement\\n\\nThe next stronger geometric step would be to \
replace the flat-torus proxy operator by a true torus Laplace--Beltrami \
operator derived from the induced metric. That would make the linearization \
geometry-dependent rather than only periodic-domain dependent.\"\>",
